.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH syncweb 1  "syncweb " 
.SH NAME
syncweb \- Delay\-tolerant web surfing
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsyncweb\fR [\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-daemon\fR] [\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-network\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Delay\-tolerant web surfing
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose structured logging
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit machine\-readable JSON. Each command prints a single JSON object (arrays only inside a named key); streaming commands (stats network \-\-follow) print one JSON object per line (NDJSON)
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Assume yes to every destructive\-operation prompt
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-daemon\fR
Bypass the daemon and use an embedded node for supported commands
.TP
\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR \fI<DATA_DIR>\fR [default: .syncweb]
Directory used for persistent node identity and data
.TP
\fB\-\-network\fR \fI<NETWORK>\fR
Network name for scoped operations (uses data_dir/<network>/). Defaults to \*(Aqdefault\*(Aq if absent.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
syncweb\-start(1)
Start the local syncweb daemon
.TP
syncweb\-stop(1)
Stop the local syncweb daemon
.TP
syncweb\-status(1)
Show local daemon status
.TP
syncweb\-reload(1)
Ask the local daemon to reload configuration
.TP
syncweb\-sync(1)
Ask the local daemon to trigger synchronization
.TP
syncweb\-devices(1)
Show this device\*(Aqs Iroh and Syncthing identities
.TP
syncweb\-folders(1)
Manage synchronized folders (bare: list managed folders)
.TP
syncweb\-ls(1)
List files in a local folder
.TP
syncweb\-stat(1)
Show detailed metadata for a local file
.TP
syncweb\-find(1)
Search local files
.TP
syncweb\-search(1)
Search catalog content, packages, and editorial channels
.TP
syncweb\-sort(1)
Sort local files by discovery criteria
.TP
syncweb\-download(1)
Download folder content or copy a local file
.TP
syncweb\-verify(1)
Re\-check local folder blob integrity
.TP
syncweb\-transfer(1)
Inspect and control durable transfer jobs
.TP
syncweb\-share(1)
Share a folder, printing a ticket (read\-only by default, \-\-write for write access)
.TP
syncweb\-access(1)
Show who can read/write each folder in one table, and revoke access in place (\-\-revoke)
.TP
syncweb\-link(1)
Create and resolve stable syncweb links
.TP
syncweb\-package(1)
Create, version, publish, and manage collection packages
.TP
syncweb\-network(1)
Manage networks and membership
.TP
syncweb\-watch(1)
Watch a folder and import filesystem changes
.TP
syncweb\-snapshot(1)
Manage content\-addressed snapshots
.TP
syncweb\-indexing(1)
Manage opt\-in indexing, catalogs, and metadata
.TP
syncweb\-stats(1)
Show statistics for folders and files
.TP
syncweb\-db(1)
Database maintenance: check, vacuum, stats, backup
.TP
syncweb\-config(1)
Show or update local configuration
.TP
syncweb\-version(1)
Show syncweb version information
.TP
syncweb\-completions(1)
Generate shell completions
.TP
syncweb\-manpages(1)
Generate manpages
.TP
syncweb\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
